# ── ⚠️ THE PLATFORM'S OWN FILES ARE NOT WEBSITE CONTENT ─────────────────────
#
# Eleventy's input directory is the repository root (see eleventy.config.js), and it publishes
# EVERY template-format file it finds under it — .md included. Nothing here was marked as a
# page, and that is the point: a .md file needs no front matter and no link to become a live
# URL, so anything dropped in this repo is published by default.
#
# That put 14 internal documents on the public web, all of them listed in sitemap.xml, all
# returning 200:
#
#   /lib/strategist-prompt/          the system prompt the assistant runs on (36KB)
#   /lib/onboarding-interview/       the onboarding script and the memory-layer design
#   /platform-kb/*  (12 pages)       Earned Media's own research and method notes
#
# ⚠️ IGNORED, NOT DELETED, AND THE DISTINCTION MATTERS. These files are read at build time by
# nothing, but scripts/ingest-platform-kb.js reads platform-kb/ straight off disk and lib/
# holds real code. `.eleventyignore` removes them from the OUTPUT only; every script that
# depends on them is unaffected.
#
# ⚠️ AND REMOVING THE PAGES IS ONLY HALF OF IT. The 14 URLs are already indexed, and a page
# that stops being generated is a page that 404s — which Google honours eventually, on its own
# schedule. Getting them out of results now needs a per-URL removal in Search Console for
# mrpaint.com.au, and the removal only sticks while the URL keeps answering 404 or 410.
#
# ⚠️ DO NOT ADD `blog`. Those 33 .md files are the real content and are meant to be published.
